  "internNote": "intern guidelines\ninterns are working solely for the opportunity of learning the trade. Accordingly, I like to give them a variety of tasks so they can learn. I find it beneficial for them to do each task twice, back-to-back if possible in order to learn through repetition. CAP is always first. Usually upright restoration CAP (twice, as mentioned), then they can move on to refurbishing, restringing, grand CAP, and possibly PRSB, though PRSB requires a lot of tutoring and supervision. DHRT (grand or upright) is usually the last task they generally have before the end of their 520 hours."
